<title>USA: Trump Hotels Q3 shr increases.</title>
<headline>Trump Hotels Q3 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Net shr profit	   $0.81   profit	 $0.20</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	   0.92   profit	  0.21</p>
<p> Net profit		19,541   profit	 2,045</p>
<p> Revs		     328,654		   94,895</p>
<p> Avg shrs	    32,287,756	     16,832,432</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Net shr loss	     $1.86   profit	 $0.13</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	   1.13   profit	  0.18</p>
<p> Net loss		  34,732   profit	 1,299</p>
<p> Revs		     649,660		  113,301</p>
<p> Avg shrs	    26,183,107	     16,828,228</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Per share figures and shares outstanding assume the conversion of Donald Trump's interest into 8,081,000 shares for the 1996 Q3, and 6,666,667 shares for 1995, and the respective weighting of those shares for the nine months ended September 30, 1996, and the inception-to-date period ended September 30, 1995.</p>
<p>Full company name is Trump Hotels &amp; Casino Resorts Inc.  </p>
<p>1996 net includes preopening expenses associated with the Trump riverboat in Indiana and the expansion of the Trump Plaza.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
